  "_comment": "The official cores: the ones this project makes, publishes and supports, and which repository publishes each one. Cores other people make are in third-party-cores.json. Chimera does NOT read this file and does not ship it - the frontend downloads nothing and lists only the packages somebody put in its Cores folder (docs/core-manager.md). It is kept in the repository for two readers: CI, which fetches each core's published package to check the frontend against it (tools/fetch-cores.sh), and the documentation, which lists where the cores are. A row carries each system's id (what movies and projects are keyed by) and the CORE'S OWN NAME for it, copied from the core's package when it joined; a test holds the row to what the packages say. \"tested\" is not used.",
